# Assignment 4.2 — Job Application Form

## Question 1: Create fields for full name, email, and phone number.

**Answer:**

```html
<label for="fullName">Full Name:</label>
<input type="text" id="fullName" name="fullName" required>

<label for="email">Email:</label>
<input type="email" id="email" name="email" required>

<label for="phone">Phone Number:</label>
<input type="tel" id="phone" name="phone" required>
```

**Explanation:** The `text`, `email`, and `tel` input types collect the applicant's name, email address, and phone number.

## Question 2: Add a date input for date of birth.

**Answer:**

```html
<label for="dob">Date of Birth:</label>
<input type="date" id="dob" name="dob" required>
```

**Explanation:** The `date` input type allows users to select a date from a calendar.

## Question 3: Add a URL input for the portfolio URL.

**Answer:**

```html
<label for="portfolio">Portfolio URL:</label>
<input type="url" id="portfolio" name="portfolio"
       placeholder="https://example.com">
```

**Explanation:** The `url` input type allows users to enter a website address. The browser checks its basic URL format when the form is submitted. This field is optional.

## Question 4: Add radio buttons for gender or preferred shift.

**Answer:**

```html
<p>Preferred Shift:</p>

<input type="radio" id="morning" name="shift" value="Morning" required>
<label for="morning">Morning</label>

<input type="radio" id="evening" name="shift" value="Evening">
<label for="evening">Evening</label>

<input type="radio" id="night" name="shift" value="Night">
<label for="night">Night</label>
```

**Explanation:** Radio buttons allow users to select only one option from a group. All related radio buttons use the same `name`, which is `shift` here.

## Question 5: Add checkboxes for skills.

**Answer:**

```html
<p>Technical Skills:</p>

<input type="checkbox" id="html" name="skills" value="HTML">
<label for="html">HTML</label>

<input type="checkbox" id="css" name="skills" value="CSS">
<label for="css">CSS</label>

<input type="checkbox" id="java" name="skills" value="Java">
<label for="java">Java</label>

<input type="checkbox" id="javascript" name="skills" value="JavaScript">
<label for="javascript">JavaScript</label>
```

**Explanation:** Checkboxes allow users to select multiple skills. All these checkboxes use the same `name="skills"` because they belong to the same group.

## Question 6: Add a dropdown for qualification or job role.

**Answer:**

```html
<label for="qualification">Highest Qualification:</label>

<select id="qualification" name="qualification" required>
    <option value="">Select your qualification</option>
    <option value="12th">12th Pass</option>
    <option value="diploma">Diploma</option>
    <option value="btech">B.Tech</option>
    <option value="graduate">Other Graduate Degree</option>
</select>
```

**Explanation:** The `<select>` tag creates a dropdown menu, and each `<option>` represents a choice.

## Question 7: Add a `<textarea>` for the cover letter.

**Answer:**

```html
<label for="coverLetter">Cover Letter:</label>

<textarea id="coverLetter" name="coverLetter"
          rows="5" cols="40"
          placeholder="Write your cover letter here"
          required></textarea>
```

**Explanation:** The `<textarea>` tag provides a larger text area for writing a cover letter or other detailed information.

## Question 8: Add a disabled field.

**Answer:**

```html
<label for="applicationStatus">Application Status:</label>

<input type="text"
       id="applicationStatus"
       name="applicationStatus"
       value="Pending"
       disabled>
```

**Explanation:** The `disabled` attribute makes the field unavailable for editing. Disabled fields are not included in the submitted form data.

## Question 9: Add a submit button.

**Answer:**

```html
<button type="submit">Submit Application</button>
```

**Explanation:** The submit button attempts to submit the form after the browser checks required fields and other built-in validation rules.

## Question 10: Create the complete Job Application Form.

**Answer:**

Save the following complete code as `job-application.html`.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <title>Job Application Form</title>
</head>

<body>

    <header>
        <h1>Job Application Form</h1>
        <p>Please fill in the details to apply for the job.</p>
    </header>

    <main>

        <form action="#" method="post">

            <!-- Personal Information -->
            <fieldset>
                <legend>Personal Information</legend>

                <label for="fullName">Full Name:</label>
                <input type="text"
                       id="fullName"
                       name="fullName"
                       placeholder="Enter your full name"
                       autocomplete="name"
                       required>

                <br><br>

                <label for="email">Email Address:</label>
                <input type="email"
                       id="email"
                       name="email"
                       placeholder="Enter your email"
                       autocomplete="email"
                       required>

                <br><br>

                <label for="phone">Phone Number:</label>
                <input type="tel"
                       id="phone"
                       name="phone"
                       placeholder="Enter your phone number"
                       autocomplete="tel"
                       required>

                <br><br>

                <label for="dob">Date of Birth:</label>
                <input type="date"
                       id="dob"
                       name="dob"
                       required>

                <br><br>

                <p>Preferred Shift:</p>

                <input type="radio"
                       id="morning"
                       name="shift"
                       value="Morning"
                       required>
                <label for="morning">Morning</label>

                <input type="radio"
                       id="evening"
                       name="shift"
                       value="Evening">
                <label for="evening">Evening</label>

                <input type="radio"
                       id="night"
                       name="shift"
                       value="Night">
                <label for="night">Night</label>

            </fieldset>

            <br>

            <!-- Professional Information -->
            <fieldset>
                <legend>Professional Information</legend>

                <label for="portfolio">Portfolio URL:</label>
                <input type="url"
                       id="portfolio"
                       name="portfolio"
                       placeholder="https://example.com">

                <br><br>

                <label for="qualification">Highest Qualification:</label>

                <select id="qualification"
                        name="qualification"
                        required>

                    <option value="">Select your qualification</option>
                    <option value="12th">12th Pass</option>
                    <option value="diploma">Diploma</option>
                    <option value="btech">B.Tech</option>
                    <option value="graduate">Other Graduate Degree</option>

                </select>

                <br><br>

                <p>Technical Skills:</p>

                <input type="checkbox"
                       id="html"
                       name="skills"
                       value="HTML">
                <label for="html">HTML</label>

                <input type="checkbox"
                       id="css"
                       name="skills"
                       value="CSS">
                <label for="css">CSS</label>

                <input type="checkbox"
                       id="java"
                       name="skills"
                       value="Java">
                <label for="java">Java</label>

                <input type="checkbox"
                       id="javascript"
                       name="skills"
                       value="JavaScript">
                <label for="javascript">JavaScript</label>

                <br><br>

                <label for="coverLetter">Cover Letter:</label>
                <br>

                <textarea id="coverLetter"
                          name="coverLetter"
                          rows="5"
                          cols="40"
                          placeholder="Write your cover letter here"
                          required></textarea>

            </fieldset>

            <br>

            <!-- Disabled Field Example -->
            <fieldset>
                <legend>Application Status</legend>

                <label for="applicationStatus">Current Status:</label>
                <input type="text"
                       id="applicationStatus"
                       name="applicationStatus"
                       value="Pending"
                       disabled>

            </fieldset>

            <br>

            <!-- Submit Button -->
            <button type="submit">Submit Application</button>

        </form>

    </main>

    <footer>
        <p>Thank you for your interest in joining our team.</p>
    </footer>

</body>

</html>
```

## Submission Requirements

1. Save the file as `job-application.html`.
2. Open the file in a browser.
3. Fill in the required fields and test the radio buttons, checkboxes, dropdown, and date input.
4. Take a screenshot of the completed form.
5. Submit the HTML file and screenshot.

**Note:** This is a front-end demonstration. The form will not save or send applications to an employer because it does not have a working backend.
